# Keep line endings LF in the working tree as well as in the repository.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows with core.autocrlf=true checks the files out as
# CRLF, and any git round-trip such as a stash rewrites them in place. The Moodle
# coding standard then reports "End of line character is invalid" and treats the
# stray \r inside multi-line strings as trailing whitespace, on files that are
# perfectly clean in the repository and in CI.
* text=auto eol=lf
